  "result": "Perfect! All 172 tests pass. I've successfully implemented voucher support:\n\n**src/invoices.js:**\n- Added `applyVoucher(invoice, { code, amount })` function:\n  - Validates status is 'draft' (NOT_DRAFT error)\n  - Checks invoice doesn't already have a voucher (VOUCHER_EXISTS error)\n  - Validates amount is a positive integer (AMOUNT_INVALID error)\n  - Stores voucher as `{ code, amount }`\n  - Returns ok(newInvoice) without mutating original\n  - Preserves all invoice fields (terms, dueDate, etc.)\n\n- Updated `invoiceTotals()` to include voucher:\n  - Returns voucher amount (0 if none applied)\n  - Calculates total = subtotal - discount + vat - voucher\n  - Clamps total at 0\n\n- Updated `addLine()` and `removeLine()` to preserve vouchers on new invoices\n\n**Error codes:**\n- VOUCHER_EXISTS \u2014 invoice can only have one voucher\n\n**Tests added (12 new):**\n- Applying voucher to draft invoice\n- Voucher reducing invoice total\n- NOT_DRAFT error for issued invoices\n- VOUCHER_EXISTS error when voucher already applied\n- AMOUNT_INVALID errors (zero, negative, decimal)\n- Non-mutation of original invoice\n- Preservation of other fields (terms, dueDate, customerId)\n- Preservation through line operations\n- invoiceTotals returns zero voucher when none applied\n\nVouchers are applied after VAT calculation, reducing the final invoice total by a fixed amount in cents. Only one voucher per invoice, and only on draft invoices.",
